.TH MUSICA 1 "November 2026" "musica 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
musica \- terminal music player with album art and a live spectrum
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B musica
.RB [ \-\-no\-mouse ]
.RB [ \-\-lang " fr|en" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B musica
is a terminal music player. It shows a folder browser and a play queue side by
side, with album art read from tags or from a nearby cover file, and a
multi-line real-time spectrum analyser.
.PP
Playback starts when a file is selected in the browser. The queue can be
edited, saved as an M3U playlist and restored later. The last folder, volume,
shuffle and repeat modes, and interface language are remembered.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-mouse
Disable mouse tracking so terminal text selection works as usual.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " fr|en"
Set the interface language. This overrides the saved language.
.TP
.B \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage and options.
.TP
.B \-\-version ", " \-v
Print the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B space
Play or pause.
.TP
.B n " / " b
Next or previous track.
.TP
.B left " / " right
Seek 5 seconds backward or forward.
.TP
.B + " / " \-
Increase or decrease the volume.
.TP
.B s " / " r
Toggle shuffle or repeat.
.TP
.B j " / " k
Move the selection down or up.
.TP
.B h " / " l
Focus the browser or the queue.
.TP
.B enter
Play the selection, open a folder, or load a playlist.
.TP
.B a " / " A
Add a file or a folder to the queue.
.TP
.B /
Search the active panel. Escape clears the search.
.TP
.B i
Show track information.
.TP
.B x
Remove the selected queue track.
.TP
.B J " / " K
Move the selected queue track down or up.
.TP
.B p " / " P
Manage playlists or add the current track to a playlist.
.TP
.B ?
Show the keyboard and mouse help.
.TP
.B L
Switch the interface language.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.PP
With the mouse, click to select, double-click to play, use the wheel to
scroll, drag the progress and volume bars, and click command buttons.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/musica/state
Last folder, volume, shuffle and repeat modes, and interface language. When
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset,
.I ~/.config/musica/state
is used.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/musica/playlists/
M3U playlists managed from the interface.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation in
.I share/doc/musica/README.md
and
.IR share/doc/musica/README.fr.md .
